WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.469
- I told my son, I'm like,

00:00:01.469 --> 00:00:04.414
when you get in trouble for
not picking up your toys,

00:00:04.414 --> 00:00:07.393
do you want me to kill you?

00:00:07.393 --> 00:00:10.127
And he completely
understood what I meant by

00:00:10.127 --> 00:00:13.199
we shouldn't just shoot people

00:00:13.199 --> 00:00:16.866
because we think they've
done something bad.

00:00:20.443 --> 00:00:23.603
- Shannon is the world, the
stars, the moon, the galaxies.

00:00:23.603 --> 00:00:26.801
- My son is the reason why I'm breathing.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:28.428
He reminds me to breathe, actually.

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.790
He tells me to take deep breaths.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.364
- And I love every moment with him.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.801
- The idea that she
could be taken from me.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:36.495
The only reaction I have is to fight that.

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:39.912
Like why would somebody take her from me?

00:00:43.055 --> 00:00:46.437
- What makes me hesitant or uncomfortable

00:00:46.437 --> 00:00:50.315
about raising another black
child in American society

00:00:50.315 --> 00:00:54.482
is that by sheer virtue of
my child having brown skin

00:00:56.283 --> 00:01:00.034
or black skin, they'll
be seen as a threat.

00:01:00.034 --> 00:01:02.567
- In our own space, at home,
there's peace, there's love.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.658
But in terms of the outside that space,

00:01:04.658 --> 00:01:06.536
and we live in a system
of white supremacy,

00:01:06.536 --> 00:01:09.129
so it's definitely uncomfortable.

00:01:09.129 --> 00:01:11.342
- It's not just police
brutality I'm worried about.

00:01:11.342 --> 00:01:14.430
I'm worried about the
system and the practices

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:17.969
and policies that put black children

00:01:17.969 --> 00:01:20.969
at a disadvantage from an early age.

00:01:24.671 --> 00:01:25.778
- Our life doesn't matter.

00:01:25.778 --> 00:01:26.890
White people are more important.

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.458
I'm not pretty, I'm not valuable.

00:01:28.458 --> 00:01:31.364
I was trying to talk to a
bunch of mothers and fathers

00:01:31.364 --> 00:01:33.071
at once, just brothers and sisters,

00:01:33.071 --> 00:01:34.897
and I was trying to get
them to say I have value.

00:01:34.897 --> 00:01:35.889
And they couldn't even say it.

00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:36.910
Some couldn't even write it down.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.136
- My heart breaks for like Tamir Rice.

00:01:39.136 --> 00:01:41.180
A child was murdered in cold blood

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:42.506
in broad daylight at a park.

00:01:42.506 --> 00:01:44.248
I saw my son in him.

00:01:44.248 --> 00:01:46.428
- I read that the four year old daughter

00:01:46.428 --> 00:01:51.366
of the man that was killed
had to console the mother.

00:01:51.366 --> 00:01:53.454
- My son's two, is about to be three.

00:01:53.454 --> 00:01:55.764
I can't imagine him
witnessing my own death.

00:01:55.764 --> 00:01:56.925
- I think there are a lot of messages

00:01:56.925 --> 00:01:58.323
that parents are taking from this.

00:01:58.323 --> 00:01:59.695
You have some that feel, oh,

00:01:59.695 --> 00:02:02.413
if I just make sure my child is educated.

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:04.844
Oh, if I just make sure my black child

00:02:04.844 --> 00:02:06.260
lives in a better neighborhood.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.913
Oh, as long as I make sure, you know,

00:02:08.913 --> 00:02:11.501
my child knows what it
is to completely comply.

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:14.019
I mean, they might as well
just say "yes, master" to me.

00:02:14.019 --> 00:02:15.345
- You do have this list of things

00:02:15.345 --> 00:02:16.884
that they tell black people to do,

00:02:16.884 --> 00:02:18.249
like, you know, always be respectful.

00:02:18.249 --> 00:02:19.663
Yes, sir, put your hands up.

00:02:19.663 --> 00:02:21.236
Don't do this, don't do that.

00:02:21.236 --> 00:02:23.716
But we know that's a lie.

00:02:23.716 --> 00:02:26.487
They kill you for no reason, literally.

00:02:26.487 --> 00:02:28.920
Just because they may, oh, I feared him.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.766
- Well, I know for the
parents around myself,

00:02:32.766 --> 00:02:35.876
we are being activated into organizing

00:02:35.876 --> 00:02:38.058
and bringing our children with us.

00:02:38.058 --> 00:02:40.993
- And let her know to take
pride, take pride in her skin,

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:45.160
take pride in her hair, take
pride in all that she is.

00:02:47.652 --> 00:02:49.364
- I don't have an answer.

00:02:49.364 --> 00:02:50.516
- I'm instilling in her

00:02:50.516 --> 00:02:53.579
what she needs to know to protect her,

00:02:53.579 --> 00:02:56.162
to reaffirm that she is mighty.

00:02:57.112 --> 00:03:01.464
So in the event that she
becomes, you know, 12, 16, 17,

00:03:01.464 --> 00:03:05.190
she's walking out in the street
and someone guns her down,

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.231
I know that that was beyond my control.

00:03:07.231 --> 00:03:09.163
- My son can die at the
hands of the police.

00:03:09.163 --> 00:03:11.363
I can die at the hands of the police.

00:03:11.363 --> 00:03:12.739
Just for being black.

00:03:12.739 --> 00:03:15.083
That's a reality that I have to live with.

00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:16.439
- My five year old, he understands.

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:20.888
He asked me, "Mommy, are you
gonna get shot by the police?"

00:03:20.888 --> 00:03:23.656
And he was playing with his
white friend around the same age

00:03:23.656 --> 00:03:26.211
and the white friend, you
know, pulls up his hand

00:03:26.211 --> 00:03:28.661
and is like, "Oh, I got
a shot by the doctor."

00:03:28.661 --> 00:03:31.294
And you can just see the disparity

00:03:31.294 --> 00:03:34.275
of the lives that they're living.

00:03:34.275 --> 00:03:37.230
- You don't think, oh, my
child can't walk to the store.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:39.477
And he's gonna die on the way back.

00:03:39.477 --> 00:03:40.519
You try not to.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:42.429
You want them to have
the best quality of life

00:03:42.429 --> 00:03:43.544
and the best quality of life isn't

00:03:43.544 --> 00:03:45.201
being like nobody can't go outside.

00:03:45.201 --> 00:03:47.368
- We don't have time to be

00:03:48.272 --> 00:03:50.997
engaged in intellectual masturbating.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:53.566
- Dealing with this system
in terms of police brutality,

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.299
we need a standard, at the federal level,

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:58.092
some type of standard protocol

00:03:58.092 --> 00:04:00.516
in which every police
department has to abide by.

00:04:00.516 --> 00:04:03.558
- I can't imagine the system
that we have right now

00:04:03.558 --> 00:04:06.534
for my son to grow up safely.

00:04:06.534 --> 00:04:09.318
- I'm gonna try my best
to share with my son

00:04:09.318 --> 00:04:12.122
the realities of his life, and hopefully,

00:04:12.122 --> 00:04:16.273
he'll be able to navigate
it with wisdom and in love.

00:04:16.273 --> 00:04:20.440
- If we just internalize and
became so aware of black power,

00:04:22.921 --> 00:04:25.444
one, we wouldn't be sitting
here trying to convince people

00:04:25.444 --> 00:04:27.108
who we are and that we have value.

00:04:27.108 --> 00:04:28.635
We'd like, okay, you know what?

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:30.297
You come see me when you're
ready to make some changes.

